      <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Top 5 Expensify Alternatives for 2026</h1>
      <p class="mb-8 text-lg text-neutral-400">Why teams are switching from Expensify to transparent, confidence-scored document extraction.</p>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
        <p>Expensify has long been a household name for expense reporting and receipt scanning. But as businesses demand more transparency from their AI tools, many are looking for Expensify alternatives that offer better visibility into accuracy, fairer pricing, and support for a wider range of documents.</p>

        <p>In this guide, we compare the top 5 Expensify alternatives for 2026, focusing on AI document extraction, receipt scanning, invoice processing, and the all-important <strong>confidence scoring</strong> that tells you exactly how reliable your extracted data is.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-100 pt-4">Why Look Beyond Expensify?</h2>
        <p>Expensify's SmartScan technology is convenient, but it has significant limitations. The biggest pain point is the lack of transparency. When Expensify extracts data from a receipt or invoice, you have no way of knowing which fields it got right and which it might have misread. You must either trust the output blindly or manually verify every single field.</p>

        <p>Other issues include expensive per-seat pricing, a 100% premium if you bring your own cloud storage (BYOC), and limited support for structured data like tables and line items. For finance teams processing hundreds of invoices monthly, these limitations add up to significant costs and wasted time.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-100 pt-4">1. PDF2DataAI</h2>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Teams that need transparent, confidence-scored document extraction for invoices, receipts, and forms.</p>
        <p>PDF2DataAI is the most transparent alternative to Expensify. Every extracted field gets a 0-100% confidence score. Fields below 90% are automatically flagged for human review. This means you only check what needs attention, reducing review time by up to 80%.</p>
        <p><strong>Key features:</strong> Per-field confidence scoring, auto-flag below 90%, smart table detection, OCR for scanned documents, multi-format export (Excel, CSV, JSON), free tier available, no BYOC penalty.</p>
        <p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Free (10 pages/mo), Pro $19/mo (500 pages), Business $49/mo (2,000 pages).</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-100 pt-4">2. Dext (formerly Receipt Bank)</h2>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Accounting firms and bookkeepers.</p>
        <p>Dext offers robust receipt and invoice processing with direct integrations to accounting software like Xero and QuickBooks. However, it lacks per-field confidence scoring and has limited support for non-receipt documents like contracts or multi-page reports.</p>
        <p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Starts at $20/month per user.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-100 pt-4">3. Rossum</h2>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Enterprise invoice processing.</p>
        <p>Rossum uses AI to extract data from invoices and offers a validation interface. It supports custom document types and integrates with ERP systems. However, pricing is enterprise-level and opaque, and confidence scoring is not as granular as per-field systems.</p>
        <p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Custom quote required.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-100 pt-4">4. Veryfi</h2>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Receipt scanning and expense management.</p>
        <p>Veryfi offers OCR-based receipt scanning with automatic categorization. It has a free tier and reasonable API pricing for developers. However, it lacks transparent confidence scoring and has limited support for table-heavy documents.</p>
        <p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Free (Basic), $15/mo (Pro), API plans available.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-100 pt-4">5. ABBYY FlexiCapture</h2>
        <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Large enterprises with complex document processing needs.</p>
        <p>ABBYY is a powerful document capture platform that handles invoices, forms, and structured documents. It offers high accuracy but comes with enterprise-level complexity and pricing. Setup requires significant IT involvement and template configuration.</p>
        <p><strong>Pricing:</strong> Custom enterprise quote.</p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-100 pt-4">Comparison Table</h2>
